---
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="About Me"
    description="about joshua and who he is"
    pubDate={new Date("August 08 2022")}
>
    <section class="about">
        <p>
            I like slow things. Quiet websites. Stories that don’t rush to
            explain themselves. Most of my time is spent reading, coding,
            watching films, or thinking about ideas that sit somewhere between
            all three.
        </p>

        <p>
            I work on the web, but what draws me in isn’t just code. It’s
            structure, rhythm, and the feeling of moving through something
            thoughtfully made. I’m drawn to interfaces that feel considered and
            humane, and to systems that are simple on the surface but layered
            underneath.
        </p>

        <p>
            This site is closer to a personal notebook than a finished showcase.
            A place to collect thoughts, fragments, experiments, and things I
            want to remember. Some pages are complete, others are still
            becoming. I like the idea that writing and ideas can live in public
            without being finalized.
        </p>

        <p>
            I’m especially interested in storytelling, memory, and routine. Many
            of my side projects lean toward small games or interactive ideas
            that explore limitation, atmosphere, and subtle change rather than
            spectacle. I care more about mood than mechanics, and more about
            implication than explanation.
        </p>

        <p>
            Outside of making things, I read widely and watch films obsessively.
            Russian literature, old paintings, quiet interiors, and long
            conversations all leave their mark on how I think. I’m drawn to work
            that feels reflective, slightly melancholic, and deeply human.
        </p>

        <p>
            I also enjoy setting up small systems for myself: media libraries,
            personal tools, little servers, and experiments that don’t need an
            audience. Not everything has to scale or ship. Some things are
            allowed to exist just because they’re useful or comforting.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you’re reading this, you’re welcome to linger. This space isn’t
            meant to impress. It’s meant to feel lived in.
        </p>
    </section>
</Layout>
